cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use renewal in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "renewal: retention, lifetime and conversion statistics for subscriptions"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/The-Commercium/renewal"
authors:
  - family-names: Demirhan
    given-names: Haluk
    affiliation: Commercium Limited
abstract: >-
  Statistics for subscription products with small samples, implemented in R, Python and
  TypeScript from one specification and checked against shared high-precision test vectors:
  shifted beta-geometric and beta-discrete-Weibull retention models for right-censored data,
  discounted expected (residual) lifetime with delta-method intervals, Jeffreys intervals for
  rates, and hierarchical beta-binomial pooling with the hyperparameters integrated out.
keywords: [retention, churn, customer lifetime value, survival analysis, subscriptions, R, Python, TypeScript]
references:
  - type: article
    authors: [{family-names: Fader, given-names: Peter S.}, {family-names: Hardie, given-names: Bruce G. S.}]
    title: "How to project customer retention"
    journal: "Journal of Interactive Marketing"
    volume: 21
    issue: 1
    start: 76
    end: 90
    year: 2007
